      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around Not My Pâté line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Неплохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not bad.' This quick response translates directly to \"not bad\" and shows a rare moment of mild approval from the chef.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Да?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Huh?' Max reacts with a single word of surprise that functions much like \"really?\" or \"yeah?\" in English conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Только это не мой паштет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Only this isn't my pâté.' Barinov drops a twist by starting with a word meaning \"only\" or \"just,\" completely crushing the young cook's hopes.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Как?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What?' The everyday word for \"how\" works perfectly here to convey total confusion and disbelief.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Та же консистенция.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Same texture.' Pointing out the physical similarities, the sentence relies on a shared borrowed word for \"consistency.\"",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "И состав я подобрал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I got the ingredients right.' Defending his culinary skills, he explains that he successfully selected or matched the recipe's composition.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Подождите.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait.' Here the polite request for \"hold on\" acts as a desperate plea for clarification.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Что входит в ваш паштет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What goes into your pâté?' Max asks about the mystery ingredients by literally questioning what \"enters into\" the dish.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Это секрет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is a secret.' Shutting down the inquiry, the reply relies on a simple statement equating the dish to a mystery.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Пойдём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's go.' With a single word meaning \"we will go,\" the head chef signals that it is time to move to another location.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Посмотрим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Take a look.' Following his previous direction, he promises they will \"look\" or \"see\" what is really going on.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good.' Yielding to his boss, the young cook uses a versatile term for \"okay\" or \"fine\" to show obedience. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
